# Your own Content delivery key. Create one in Content -> Configure -> Delivery,
# in an ebitex organization you control.
#
# For local development an unrestricted key is fine. For a deployed site use a
# BROWSER-SAFE key restricted to your own origin -- the key ships inside the
# JavaScript bundle, so anyone can read it. See the README, step 3.
VITE_CONTENT_DELIVERY_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the ebitex production API (https://api.ebitex.io).
# VITE_CONTENT_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional optimization. Pin the site so the SDK skips its discovery call on
# first load. Find it in Content -> Configure -> Delivery, under your site.
# VITE_CONTENT_SITE_ID=

# The contact page embeds a form from ebitex Forms. Both are optional: without
# them the page renders a short note instead of an empty iframe.
#
# Your organization's slug, which appears in every public form URL.
# VITE_FORMS_ORG_SLUG=

# Where Forms is served from. Defaults to the ebitex production Forms app.
# VITE_FORMS_BASE_URL=

# ---- build-time only, never shipped to the browser ----
#
# Two things read this: scripts/sitemap.mjs at build time, and `npm run codegen`
# from your terminal. Both run outside a browser, so both use a SERVER-SIDE key.
# Note the missing VITE_ prefix: that prefix is exactly what decides whether a
# value is inlined into the JavaScript bundle, so this one stays private.
#
# A browser-safe key will NOT work here -- it is restricted by Origin, and Node
# sends no Origin header, so the request is refused.
# CONTENT_DELIVERY_KEY=
# CONTENT_SITE_ID=
# SITE_ORIGIN=https://your-site.example
